cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, cite it as below."
title: "Proteus: a closed-loop network defense driven by a simulated C. elegans connectome"
abstract: >-
  A deterministic C99 simulator of a 279-neuron C. elegans connectome
  (graded potentials, short-term synaptic plasticity, neuromodulators,
  body physics) drives the port schedule and firewall actions of a network
  daemon, so that the defense is a readout of nervous-system state rather
  than a seeded PRNG. The release ships preregistered hypotheses,
  falsification criteria and negative results alongside the code.
authors:
